  <content>
  <section><para>Here is a graph of a function \(w\) defined by \(w(x)=(x+1.6)(x-2)\). Three points on the graph are labeled.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/74b2c12481cf4b589d93d52105cae863756c18dc"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Use the graph to answer the following questions.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="dcaecaca-551f-4428-b461-397612b1b26c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(a\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -1.6</para><para>The correct answer is -1.6.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ce7be0ea-3f67-4b38-83a3-2d3236f4b535" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(b\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0</para><para>The correct answer is 0.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="27d60512-5982-460e-b522-58cdcdf44e23" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(c\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 2</para><para>The correct answer is 2.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="1c23d2c3-40ef-43e2-a2c8-733c481fa5aa" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(d\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0</para><para>The correct answer is 0.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="8ae82ca8-9dda-4ca2-a107-d575990b42e5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(e\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0</para><para>The correct answer is 0.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="c1d3952f-c6e2-4b1a-82e1-c67eda6408d7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the value of \(f\). Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -3.2</para><para>The correct answer is -3.2.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
